# Rule - Definition of Done (DoD)

## Completion checklist

A user story or feature must meet **all** applicable items below before it may be marked done. Scope: one story at a time (`incremental-delivery`). Quality bar: `common-test-strategy` (referenced under **Quality met**).

## Code & toolchain

- [ ] Unit and integration tests for the changed behavior pass locally
- [ ] Lint / formatter clean on touched files (when the project defines them)
- [ ] Typecheck passes (when the project uses static types)
- [ ] No new critical static-analysis or security findings introduced by the change (when tooling exists)

## Feature usable

- [ ] All acceptance criteria (AC) are implemented (where applicable)
- [ ] Frontend and backend APIs are integrated and verified end-to-end
- [ ] Error handling is implemented
- [ ] Edge cases are handled
- [ ] All interfaces use real, working integrations — no mock data unless the user explicitly allows it
- [ ] Pause and ask the user: “Do you confirm this feature is usable?” Continue only after explicit approval

## Quality met

- [ ] Meet **100%** of the applicable items in the **Common Test Strategy** quality checklist (`common-test-strategy`)
- [ ] If the project defines its own test strategy / quality standards, also meet **100%** of those — they must **comply with and not weaken** the common strategy
- [ ] Prefer the stricter bar when both apply

## Version control (when the workflow expects it)

- [ ] Changes committed with a clear message **only when the user requested a commit or project DoD requires it** (do not commit unprompted)
- [ ] No secrets, credentials, or stray temp files in the commit
- [ ] Branch pushed to remote when the team’s DoD or release process requires it

## Docs in sync

- [ ] Requirements spec updated (if changed)
- [ ] Design spec updated (if changed)
- [ ] UI spec updated (if changed)
- [ ] API docs updated (where applicable)
- [ ] README updated (where applicable)

## Retrospective

Run the `retrospective` skill before marking the work done (after the items above are satisfied, or as the final DoD gate).

- [ ] Retrospective completed for this feature / task
- [ ] ADR-worthy decisions persisted under `specs/adr/` — or explicitly recorded that none were ADR-worthy
- [ ] Knowledge-worthy lessons persisted under `specs/knowledge/` — or explicitly recorded that none were knowledge-worthy
- [ ] Retrospective Summary presented (ADRs created, knowledge added/updated, items skipped)

An empty retrospective is valid when nothing is durable enough to persist — still run the skill and state that clearly. Do not skip the gate.

## How to use this rule

**During development**

- Treat this checklist as the working guide; do not skip sections

**When claiming done**

- Check every applicable item; mark complete only when all pass
- If any item fails, keep working until it passes

**At acceptance**

- User and developer confirm the checklist together
- Record acceptance time and accepter when the project requires it
